487:* `I1` The face intent plane (#/rulings, the channel of intent, 2026-10-20; <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">>). Build order, each step red-first: `@intents-<tag>` minted by the PersonaGroup with its entry kinds (intent, outcome, asks and answer, claim, release and takeover, supersede and cancel), each signed by its device's atom and its id a content hash; stand-down and the three verb classes, with a single-effect verb addressed to "any device" refused at issue; the read-side winner; causal voids and the operator's release; the face-join summons moving off the daemon doc onto the plane, which closes two hearths of one face, beside the CLI naming its face per invocation; the daemon wiki's view pane; the rubric's witness (a hundred keystrokes and a save write no entry; one move writes one intent and one outcome); then the far agent's relay seat after its own research. Its reds stand at the carrier's #/the-reds. Its authority reads stand on the face's sealed identity anchor, so it builds after Wave C lands the anchor (operator, 2026-10-20, approving the controller's lean); the relay seat's own research wave follows it. Lead: a Sonnet Episkopos with a Sol and a Copilot seat. I.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-d-lane.mem:40:# ''The seat lands when the grant arrives'': one serialized seat act owns the later grant's take, verify, ingest and the floor lift, with one in-flight promise, so duplicate wakes coalesce and a wake that lands mid-act earns one trailing pass. Three causal wakes feed it and nothing else: a change on the retained PersonaGroup document, filtered to this vessel's `face-join-grant/v1` title; a daemon-layer change under the group's lease prefix, and, only while a grant waits unjudged on an unavailable lease frontier, any daemon-layer change (a late layer wakes it even when it holds no lease slot, since the composite forwards a joining layer's records as changes); and one replay at boot once the lease listener attaches. The PersonaGroup document listener attaches when that plane arrives and replays the act once, so a boot never waits on an unsynced plane and no grant falls between the boot pass and the listener. A signature reads judged only after its ingest lands (a definitive verify refusal judges once per boot); an ingest fault, or a lease frontier that reads unavailable, leaves the record unjudged for the next causal change. No clock, no poll, no retry timer. `faceSeated` reports `knowsAgent` and takes nothing; vessel-only reuse reads the record and returns it; the mint path waits for the seat act before it reads the seat. The binding rests in D, in the face subtree, never in the floor index. Reds: a grant arriving after a vessel-only binding seats and lifts with no binding call (control: no grant, the floor stays); a grant before the daemon layer stays unjudged until the layer's join seats it; duplicate pulses ingest once; an ingest fault then a later change still seats; a crash between ingest and lift finishes once at restart.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:33:''The Council's lease never runs backward.'' A stale replica of the Council's daemon doc arrives missing the newest lease slot. Before Wave C, an old device edge reads current against it. After it, each device keeps a sealed frontier that never falls, and the stale replica moves nothing.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:47:# ''The sealed anchor.'' Each face holds, on each device, a D row: its PersonaGroup, persona-KEL prefix, a commitment to its root, its edge's digest, and a known frontier that never falls. Founding, admission and the recovery rites write it; sync never does. Red: a forged selector row in the daemon doc, then a coherent valid foreign bundle, switch no pinned face; a missing anchor refuses face boot by name.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:49:# ''The monotone frontier.'' Lease advances carry signatures in the per-writer shape (`lease-advance`: each writer signs `{resource, writer, epoch}` into its own slot); the sealed local frontier never falls. A lease advance rides a per-writer signed slot and never the `@persona` log, since two writers advancing at once would fork a hash-linked log, and the house names forks and never resolves them; per-writer slots let concurrent writers both land while the max climbs. A face's advance is `lares persona lease`, and the boot raises the anchor only from slots that verify (`lease-observation`). Red: a deleted, replayed or unsigned high slot lowers nothing and raises nothing. An act that widens authority (admit, grant, re-key, seal to a reader) refuses a target naming a newer bound than the frontier holds, its receipt naming the frontier it acted under.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:62:!! Beside it ~ the edge frontier
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:64:Row `K17`, the signed edge frontier (#/rulings, the edge frontier), shares Wave C's signed-log pattern and builds beside it: the frontier certificate, the genesis frontier at every founding, raise registration, the widening reader, and the admit bundle carrying the frontier. Wave C's anchor and `K17`'s frontier read one verifier style on node and browser.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:80:* ''The recovery door: guardian-quorum rotation, then `reanchorAfterRotation`, then a re-admit carrying the log and frontier.'' No production door rotates a persona root beneath its KEL prefix: `reanchorAfterRotation` stands proven as a library function with its red and control (a face recovered to a new root boots against the rewritten anchor; a document naming the new root with no KEL rotation behind it refuses), and `runReadmitEdge` has no production caller. Building the door means the guardian-quorum ceremony, whose guardian count is an open operator gate (`kahu#/seed-and-nexus`). The re-admit then carries the current `@persona` log and the signed frontier as a first admit does.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:84:* ''The retired-key window after a lost-and-recovered offline device'': an act beyond a reader's accepted frontier signs under the KEL's current epoch, and a lease advance counts only from the current roster. A legitimate act or advance signed under the old epoch that this reader had not yet accepted therefore needs re-signing under the new epoch; the recovery door (K18) owns that re-sign.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:88:* ''The holder's teardown backstop'' keeps one five-second timer that completes a teardown whose island never acknowledged. It decides nothing about identity, a frontier or a greeting; the house is already ended when it fires.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:91:* ''The fleet frontier's pin lives in the vessel's own mutable ledger'' (read 4's LEAD against `edge-frontier-board.ts` and `edge-kapae.ts`): a vessel that loses that ledger and then reads a stale board under an older valid frontier reads an absent edge as clear. A reader with a pin refuses a board that does not extend it (`does-not-extend-pin`, red in `edge-frontier.test.ts`), and a vessel with no pin at all is a fresh one, which cannot tell a stale board from a young fleet. Pinning the fleet head in the sealed anchor, beside the act head and the lease, belongs to K17.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:92:* ''Read 5's remaining MEDIUMs'' (5 HIGH cured in the lane, MEDIUMs named, none authority-bearing past the proof): the admit preflight checks that a frontier record exists but leaves its signed hand, group, roster and snapshot to the later boot's reader (`ceremony-core.ts`); the issuer stamps the signed admission's epoch from the raw chain head, where the verified lineage's last epoch would match (`device-admit.ts`); the fleet-join offer reads its group through `facePersonaGroup` from the bootstrap on the founding face (`fleet-join.ts`) and `init.ts` reads the bootstrap group to choose `alreadyStood`; a holder session whose lock or proof rejects after the greeting leaves queued asks waiting without a named refusal (`shared-holder.ts`); the browser's second face neither joins nor proves its identities and circles documents (Wave D slice 4). Each rides its owning lane's row: K17 for the frontier verification, K15-H for the Handle owner, Wave D for the browser faces.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:93:* ''Read 6's two lane-owned HIGH, written verbatim as Wave D's opening rows'' (read 6 found no P0: an unaffiliated wire peer reached no face act and no private plane). ROW 1: MEASURED — lane-owned composition, foreign face share falls open when its catalog row is absent. `packages/lararium-node/src/face-fleet-view.ts:76-87,131-137`; `packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:753-754`. One-line reason: the worn face bridge allows *every* document id outside a negative set derived from the mutable catalog, so deleting or withholding a foreign face's row before a new session is seated removes that face's private plane from the deny set. This is the exact inverse of the proposed authority direction: an unverified catalog *absence* changes a share from false to true. The `bb8513247` repair added `foreignFaceDocs`, but the live verdict is `view.fetch(id).ok || !others.has(id)`; a missing catalog entry makes `others.has` false. The source test itself demonstrates the relevant behavior at `face-fleet-view.test.ts:122-140`: with only the worn bootstrap, the bare bridge reads the other face's circles, and supplying a catalog-derived `foreign` set blocks it. The control never tries the catalog row deleted after registration, or a held other-face document whose catalog entry was omitted. A same-operator session of the worn face can fetch the other face's held document by id in that state. The verdict is wired through `shareConfigOf` to both the announce and access hooks (`federation-gate.ts:602-611`), so this is an access decision rather than an announcement-only cosmetic leak; the live transport control at `share-policy-is-access.test.ts:49-67` demonstrates that distinction. This is not P0 under the user's definition because the reader already has an admitted face; the leak crosses face compartments on one vessel. The authorization decision must come from the sealed/proven face-document inventory or a positive view, rather than catalog completeness. The broad bridge predates Wave C (Wave B/O1), but Wave C owns the `foreignFaceDocs` repair and its composer wiring; this finding concerns that lane-owned repair, not the inherited bridge in isolation. ROW 2: MEASURED — lane-owned node daemon keeps a lease floor older than the sealed anchor it raises at boot. `packages/lararium-node/src/open-node-vessel.ts:2260-2271,2311-2346`; `packages/lararium-keyhive/src/operator-daemon-behavior.ts:306-321,421-423,704-743,986-1008`; `packages/lararium-keyhive/src/lease-frontier.ts:64-70`. One-line reason: the composer snapshots `standingAnchor` into `daemonAuth` and awaits `openDaemonVm` *before* it raises and persists the verified lease epoch; the running daemon's live join and grant reads keep flooring under the old object. For a concrete counterexample, start with sealed lease epoch 0 and a verified signed advance to 7 in the mirrored daemon doc. The daemon receives anchor 0, starts, then the parent persists anchor 7 at `:2346`. If that mutable slot is deleted or replayed to 0 during the same daemon lifetime, `readLeaseUnderFace` reads 0 and floors against the daemon's captured anchor 0, despite custody now pinning 7. Its live face-join at `operator-daemon-behavior.ts:704-743` passes the lowered `lease.n` into a new seat and re-seal, while grant ingest at `:306-321` verifies an older bound. A restart loads 7 and closes the window; the claim that the sealed frontier never falls in a standing daemon does not hold. This is Wave C's lease-observation and composer ordering, not an inherited timer. The seam should raise the anchor before forming/sending `daemonAuth`, or deliver the raised pin to the daemon through a verified update. The existing red at `signed-lease-frontier.test.ts:50-61` hands `readLeaseUnderFace` an anchor already at 7, and `lease-observation.test.ts:26` tests the pure raise, so both can pass while the composer sends 0 before it persists 7. A red needs the live daemon, a signed advance, a subsequent slot deletion, and a control that the older edge or grant remains refused without restart.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k15-wave-c-lane.mem:94:* ''The realm leg'' is its own lane, K17-R (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/k17-realm-lease-lane">>): one lease law on the realm boards, landed after Wave C.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/automerge-tiga.mem:68:| `IntentsDoc` | `@intents-<tag>` | the face's channel of intent: intents, outcomes and asks across its fleet, append-only, never mirrored (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane">>) |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:69:''A spirit holds a seat and no key'' (operator ruling, 2026-10-12; quote license: //"the spirit's identity enacts the operator's relationship"//; //"you all get a 'seat' here in the lararium … your persona's don't trade keys out, the vessel itself serves as your identity-as-relation across all AI frontier model providers and locally run models later"//). The seat rests on the vessel. A model from any provider, or a model run locally, may sit in it, and none carries it away. A spirit's persona names who authored; it never names who signed.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/session-contract.mem:236:''A missing record proves no clean history.'' A device's own gate enforces its standing best-effort; its peers' gates enforce it, each from its own ledger and the signed standing it holds. A peer reads a device's absent raise against the board's signed edge frontier (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road">> #/rulings, the edge frontier): holding a frontier that includes every raise it has seen, it reads absence as clear as of that frontier; lacking one, a widening act waits as unknown. Until the frontier stands built, a peer reads absence as clear for sync and for widening alike, and the gap stays named.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/convergent-mesh.mem:45:* ''Automerge logical time'' — carries causal order + fork-detection (`getHeads`/`headsEqual`; a partitioned frontier `drifted` stands as a fork).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:82:# ''The presentation follows in the first encrypted frames.'' A face's presentation carries the face's public key, the vessel's face-scoped key with its certificate, the session key with its certificate, ONE presentation arm (an admit, a hosting grant, or an invite claim) and that arm's causal lineage, and the presenter's withdrawal frontier with any events the gate may lack (#/the-withdrawal-proof). An admit's `nym` MUST equal the face key. No ContactCard, no vessel key, no persona root, no root edge, no identifier shared across faces, and by default no Handle rides it.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:126:> ''House ruling under the operator's delegation'' (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/stable-founding-road#/rulings">>); it reopens on proof that a gate pin decides no authority anywhere.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:200:* ''A household TLS terminator, its log's reader, or a herm that sees the upgrade, once it holds candidate sovereign gate pins, learns which Nexus a dial selects among the K gates sharing its address and route (at most log2(K) bits per dial, none where K=1) and links that Nexus's repeat visits; the knock never tells it the presenting face, the admission verdict or any sealed byte.'' The operator's ruling of 2026-10-26 places this reader outside the sovereign route's promise. A sovereign pin escaping its members' custody, or a ruling that extends route confidentiality to pin-holders, reopens `W10` (the reading and its measurements stand at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w28-gate-lane">> #/the-knock-reading).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:227:''The frontier names how much history a party holds'': a position and the head at that position. Every presentation carries its presenter's frontier, and the signed finish covers it, so a presenter cannot later disown the frontier it showed. A presenter ahead of the gate carries the events the gate lacks.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:234:| `verified` | every signature and binding holds, the presenter's frontier meets the gate's own, and no learned denial names the key | it attaches the session, and keeps any events the presenter carried | it acts |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:235:| `unconfirmed` | the chain holds and no learned denial names the key, and the gate holds a later frontier than the presenter showed | it attaches nothing and hands over the events the presenter lacks | it acts on nothing shared, folds the events, and presents again under the later frontier |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:237:| `incomplete` | the presenter names a frontier the gate cannot join to its own: a later one with events missing, or another head at a position the gate holds | it abstains and asks for the history from its genesis | it carries the whole history |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:243:''A gate's learned state only accretes.'' Learning reads as a union of verified events, whatever order they arrive in. An older frontier never replaces a later one, a denial once counted keeps counting through a fork and after it, and a fork once proven stays proven. A presentation that carries one event the gate cannot verify teaches the gate nothing.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:269:| a withdrawn vessel that shows an older frontier | nothing at a gate that holds the denial: the denial names its key whatever frontier it claims. At a gate that never learned, the row above | the same |
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:347:* ''The subjects'' (`packages/lararium-mesh/src/face-proof-subjects.ts`): the typed keys, the scope, the certificate and its request, the withdrawal event, the frontier, the session certificate, every signed image, and a reader for each. Every key and signature passes the one door (`ed25519-door.ts`); the purposes stand in the domain table (`domains.ts`).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-proof.mem:372:* ''The sealed frames' layout'': the frame that carries the gate's handshake reply, and the frames that carry a presentation, a frontier and the events beside it. They ride binary WebSocket messages no proxy reads; the layout in `gate-exchange.ts` stands as the house's own; the cutover has landed, and roadmap row `W28` freezes it before the founding bake.
