bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae.mem:106:the membership sense stands ''built at the edge grain'' (`edge-kapae`). Acts accrete, each keyed by edge, gesture and its own content id, so a raise and a lower written from one causal frontier both survive a merge. Each act cites its causal parents, and the fold reads the ''causal heads'' of an edge: the acts no other act cites. No version number, arrival order or clock ranks one head over another.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae.mem:108:''ONLY A FRONTIER OF LOWERS LIFTS THE SHADOW.'' A lower that causally follows every raise takes the marker down. A raise beside a lower with no causal order between them reads //unsettled// and ''leaves the shadow UP'' (remove-wins): a lower never lifts a removal by racing it. The place shows the fork, and a later act that cites both heads settles it by a deliberate hand. A frontier that cites a parent the reader lacks, or holds an act whose id fails its own bytes, proves no lift, so the shadow stays up there too. Forged acts drop before the fold; an act counts only under a hand that holds the edge (#/edge-hands), and only when its id derives from its signed bytes. An edge no act names reads //absent// and carries no shadow.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae.mem:171:* ''Every roll writes an edge anchor'' on each realm board standing under the Nexus that rolls (#/edge-hands). The quorum of the epoch the roll opens signs the closed epoch's id, the closed epoch's seated keys and threshold, the causal heads of the quorum acts that counted at the closed epoch, and the anchor that opened it. The closed keys never sign an anchor, since they may stand as the reason for the roll. The anchor follows the carriage board's roll anchor in shape and law (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lararium/mesh/membership-doctrine#/the-invite">>).
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae.mem:172:* ''A two-vault edge anchor crosses per realm.'' `lares nexus seal anchor --edge --out <partial>` opens one signed partial for each realm board under the closed charter, and `--from` judges each against the receiving vault's own board before signature and before landing. A vault with no board for that realm answers `unavailable`; a moved head answers `stale`; an anchor that already counts answers `replay`. The answer names each realm `anchored` or `owed`. The signed image follows `signEdgeRollAnchor`.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/orichalcum-capabilities.mem:194:note    = "capability invalid once the chain rolls past the epoch it roots on. An ORDER, never an instant — a reader RANKS it by walking the chain it holds, and an unwalkable epoch ranks below every known one (fail-closed). Built: delegation-edge + edge-kapae. Distinct from the integer lease frontier (carrier A, epoch-lease/boundEpoch) only in how the order is carried; same law"
