bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/face-intent-plane.mem:47:* ''A fifth face plane'', `@intents-<tag>`, beside `@persona`, `@circles`, `@identities` and `@sessions` (<<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/automerge-tiga">>). It derives from the PersonaGroup's tag like its siblings, so every device that joins the face derives its name and syncs it with no extra provisioning; two faces on one device share no entry; nothing stands above it. The PersonaGroup mints it and delegates append to each device edge; the mint order binds as for every face plane.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:202:* ''The ONLY name that federates PUBLICLY ~ the public glamour'' (persona-glamour). The persona's veiled key ''signs a HandleCard'' whose `glamour` shows a chosen display (never a legal identity); it ''announces onto the per-Nexus @crossroads WHO board'' (who-face), self-certifying and causally linked. ''What supersedes it is a verified settled frontier'' — a reader folds complete causal ancestry, retains concurrent heads rather than choosing an arrival or numeric winner, and never consults a shared now. A later local freshness observation may describe liveness, but it never changes causal validity.
bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/sensorium-machina.mem:527:The producer's exact bytes and their positions enter custody before any parser speaks. A parser's block ''occurrence'' binds source, immutable byte revision, parser identity and position; a separate digest witnesses the emitted text. An observation says which revision a source exposed at a named horizon. A typed ledger records that interpretation without turning its block key into a content hash. An owned Content view then projects those blocks under an explicit model identity and a separate completion frontier. The names keep retry, reparse, duplicate text and A→B→A honest without making a parser output stand in for the original bytes.
